On Feb 26, 9:18 am, purple arcanist <ejg_...@yahoo.com> wrote:
> I would like some help with my wizard.  How do I survive in the early
> game?  Once, I survived, but that is because I started with a ring of
> regeneration and a ring of slow digestion.  Should I just not get
> within melee range (that is hard), use Elbereth, or what?
>

Make sure you have one (preferably more) of

1. A good pet
2. A bunch of daggers/ poisoned darts
3. magic missile

at all times, because wizards are crappy melee fighters. Do *NOT* let
your starting pet die or abandon it. I often play pacifist on the top
few levels, staying close to my pet to pick up fresh corpses, just so
my pet can level itself. If your dog starts to attack a powerful foe,
whistle it or yank on a leash.

To get 2, it should suffice to get a large dog/cat and enter the first
level of the mines. Engrave Elbereth on the upstairs, in dust if
nothing better, and let your pet kill everything that moves. When the
dust clears, you should have plenty of daggers and some halfway decent
armor.

Once you have at least six (preferably ten or more) daggers, forget
force bolt and try on some mithril. Raid a vault or two to get enough
gold for two+ units protection, then put on a full set of dwarvish
gear. You should have roughly AC -5 or less. If you don't, it is worth
performing a price ID on dropped dwarvish gear to identify stuff like
+2 iron shoes or a +3 dagger to wield. Now you can be a dagger chucker
and should hopefully survive early game.

As for stuff you shouldn't do, *don't* ditch your pet, *don't* let
your pet die fighting the Minetown watch, and most of all, don't
descend past Minetown without telepathy, -5 AC, and a good ranged
attack. A single polymorph trap or mind flayer could ruin your game.

> How do I get that early wish, so I can get the Staff of Ascaliptus(sp,
> the healer quest artifact)?  That would really help.  I would also
> want the PYEC.(magic marker recharge time!)
>
> I would also like a couple of tips for the late game.

If you want to wish for artifacts, don't sacrifice past Magicbane.
Instead, throw gems at unicorns to increase your luck. If you get more
artifacts, it will make artifact wishing much more difficult once you
get the castle wand. You will not need the PYEC, because once a wizard
maximizes his/her luck there's a 97% chance of writing any scroll or
book he *doesn't even recognize yet*. You can write scrolls of
charging without ever having seen a scroll of charging. You can write
a cursed scroll of genocide to get silver dragon scale mail once you
have cold resistance. You get the picture.

Speaking of artifact wishes, though the Staff of Aesculapius is a
wonderful weapon, it's not necessary. Magic missile is an incredibly
powerful spell and can serve as a wizard's main offense once he
obtains the Eye and is past level 10. Once you get the castle wand and
have the Eye, if you want the most powerful offense you can get, just
cursed-genocide wraiths a few times to get close to EXP:30, which will
raise magic missile damage past anything the staff could dream of.
You'll average approximately 45 points of damage per hit!


